## DISK AND LOAD
`df -k` at Step 0 and before every clone, build and census chunk; under 26214400 KiB available: `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY disk <n> GiB`, nothing deleted. **Small:** ONE clone (`.tools/b1198/repo`), no `npm ci` if the lock allows it: `.tools/wt-b1130-head/web/node_modules` is cloned by `cp -Rc` (APFS clone; Turbopack refuses a symlinked `node_modules`) into each tree ONLY IF `package-lock.json` there `cmp`-equals the landing tree's (blob `81393fd7...`); else ONE `npm ci` in the landing tree and clone from it. `npm ls --depth=0` rc 0 in each tree. One `.next` per tree; screenshots stay in process; `du -sk` and `df -k` around each clone and build.
**RULE L - LOAD (the ONE load rule; steps and severity point here and add none).** (i) **START:** every heavy start (clone, install, build, test, e2e, plants, EVERY census chunk) first takes a free `mkdir '.tools/heavy-slot-N'` (N 1-3, holder `B1198 <time> <label>`, released by MOVE) once load1 reads under 7 on **two reads two minutes apart** (your `hv.sh` copy). **One browser context and page at a time, never beside a build.** **The census is run in chunks, each its own start with its own 120-minute window** (RULE C below). A wait is not a finding. A chunk whose window ends NOT RUN gets **ONE fresh 120-minute window** (the round-2 gate's ruled second window, written here so you do not wait for an addendum); a second NOT RUN bars a GO and is quoted with both `rulel.txt` lines. Do not run a chunk outside the gate. (ii) **RUNNING:** a start under way is never stopped for load; load1 goes into the heartbeat. (iii) **A RED or a flagged cell:** re-run ALONE on a fresh page 3 times at the landing tree and at main: green 3 of 3 = Note "red only under load"; 1-2 of 3 = Note "unstable" (Major if a new row); 3 of 3: green at main = Blocker, red at both = Note. (The round-2 census read 9 false NEW edges at load1 11.65; every one was green 3 of 3 alone.) **Locks:** `.tools/.git-lock` (your `lock.sh` copy) wraps the fetch only; heavy jobs take the slot.
**RULE C - CHUNKS.** Order: Step 0, 1, controls of 3.1 and 4, 2, 6, then the trip census (4), the ring census (3.2), 5, 7, 8. Chunks: trips = 2 roles x 3 height ranges (390-518, 520-710, 712-900 every 2 px) = 6; ring = 8 role-and-menu groups x main then landing = 16; each is one `hv.sh` job writing `logs/<label>.rc`. Under time pressure cut from the bottom (never 3.1, 4, 5, 7 plants of the panel and the lift); a verdict without steps 3, 4, 5 and 7 finished is conditional.

## RULE T - A RING THE MENU TOGGLE COVERS (carried from B1130, "the gate's reading")
**Edge clear** = 3 ring pixels on the edge's middle line, each at 3:1 or more; the words fail in any cell with an edge not clear, whoever covers it. **T-a** cut at main too, rows not fewer: Note, counted. **T-b NEW** (clear at main, not at the landing tree): 0 rows or a pair under 3:1 in a shipped frame = **Blocker**; 1-2 rows in a drawer cell = **Major**; a frame no device ships = Note, frame stated. **Shipped frames:** widths 390, 768, 844 (drawer), 1024 and up; heights 390 and up. **E** = clear edges per cell; print cells with E_landing <, =, > E_main and rows lost on an edge main had at 3; write better, worse or mixed. Round 2 read: T-b 0 after re-runs, 15 drawer cells under the toggle with the middle line clear (Note).

## RULE B - WHAT "BROKEN" MEANS NOW (decided HERE; replaces the round-2 definitions (c), (e), (f))
**Why:** the round-2 head scrolled the PAGE to give the focused item its 6 px; the product owner's ruling moves that to the menu panel (the rail), so the scroll box changed by design. Measured against main's own scroll, nearly every trip now "differs" (the builder reads 7625). That count compares the wrong thing. **The property is:** (1) the PAGE never moves because a key was pressed inside the menu; (2) the focused item is wholly visible with its ring; a rail scroll of any size that achieves (2) is allowed.
**Frame words.** *Press:* one real `keyboard.press` of Tab or Shift+Tab with focus on a control INSIDE the rail (`aside[aria-label="Primary navigation"]`) that lands on another control inside it. *Trip:* the first rail control focused once by script, Tab to the last rail control, Shift+Tab back to the first. *Entry:* the press that moves focus from outside into the rail. *Grown box:* a control's border box grown 5 px each side (the ring reaches offset 2 + width 3).
| Id | Property per press or trip | Grade if broken in a shipped frame |
|---|---|---|
| B-1 PAGE | the document's scroll after the press (and after an entry press) equals before it | Blocker |
| B-2 SEEN | the focused control's grown box lies wholly inside the rail's client box AND inside the window; where the rail can scroll no further, the control's own box is inside and the ring rows on the edge nearest the limit are 3 (RULE T pixels) | Blocker |
| B-3 TRAVEL | Tab never scrolls the rail up and Shift+Tab never scrolls it down | Major |
| B-4 NEEDLESS | a press onto a control whose grown box is already wholly inside the rail does not scroll the rail | Major |
| B-5 ROOM | a press onto a control whose grown box is out of the rail box by 12 px or less scrolls the rail by at most (that amount + 7 px) | Major |
| B-6 RETURN | at the end of a trip the document is where the trip began AND the first control meets B-2 | Blocker |
Printed as Notes, never verdict inputs: **rail residue** (a trip ending with the rail's own scrollTop not at its start: count, size, and the element(s) lying above the first control inside the rail and their px, by name); **OLD-DEF** (the round-2 definitions against main: (c) a scroll over one item height plus 6 px beyond main's; (e) a down-then-up trip not returning where main's does; (f) a scroll for an item already 6 px or more inside at main) so the two readings can be compared; main's own B-1 count (main scrolls the page by design).
**Controls that can fail (fire first):** the round-2 merged head (`-pre`) must read B-1 above 0 with direct 1, 3 and 5 px page scrolls at press-onto-current-item cells (if 0: the instrument is blind: STOP); main must read B-1 above 0 (it scrolls the page); the landing tree with a 40 px `scroll-margin-block` plant (m5) must read B-5 above 0; the landing tree with the panel 3 px taller than the space under the top bar (h2) must read B-1 above 0.

